            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As we move our gaze through a complex scene, the retinal image is constantly shifted and overwritten. A new study using human intracranial recordings offers a fresh perspective on how the brain creates a sense of perceptual continuity through natural visual behavior.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Published by Elsevier Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
